  "description": "<p><strong>Tickets for ZSL London Zoo</strong><br>\n🎫&nbsp;Adult (16-64)<br>\n🎫 Child (3-15)<br>\n🎫 Senior (65+)/Student/Disabled (valid ID)</p>\n\n<p><em>All tickets include access to the zoo.&nbsp;Kids under 3 and carers of disabled visitors get in free.</em></p>\n\n<p><strong>Highlights</strong><br>\n⭐ Visit one of London's most popular, historic attractions&nbsp;<br>\n🦁 Get up close and personal with the mighty Asiatic lions at the <em>Land of the Lions&nbsp;</em><br>\n🦍 Visit the <em>Gorilla Kingdom</em> and see the family of silverback gorillas<br>\n🐒&nbsp;Be transported to the lush forest of Central Africa at <em>Monkey Valley</em><br>\n🦓 Over 750 species of animals to see&nbsp;<br>\n🍌 Talks and feeding sessions throughout the day&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>General Info</strong><br>\n📅 Date: various dates (select during purchase)&nbsp;<br>\n🕒 Opening hours: 10 a.m. - 4 p.m. every day.&nbsp;Last admission is 1 hour before closing time<br>\n📍 Location: London Zoo&nbsp;<br>\n👤 Age requirement: all ages welcome.&nbsp; Under 16s must be accompanied by an adult&nbsp;<br>\n♿ Accessibility: the zoo is wheelchair accessible&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Description</strong><br>\nSet in leafy Regent's Park amid heritage-listed buildings and beautiful gardens, London Zoo is an oasis in the heart of the capital with just under 15,000 amazing animals to discover, making it one of the most famous zoos in the world. Built by Victorian gentlemen with names like Sir Stamford Raffles and Decimus Burton, it's been an important part of London life for almost 200 years. With these London Zoo tickets, you'll be able to take in over 750 species of animals while walking through its historic buildings and grounds. It's the perfect day out for all ages!&nbsp;Get your tickets now for&nbsp;<em>ZSL London Zoo!</em></p>",
